<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomochichi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1644–1739</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomochichi was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamacraw">Yamacraw</a>, a small Creek-affiliated band living on a bluff above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a> River. He welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-oglethorpe">James Oglethorpe</a> in 1733, allowing the founding of Savannah, and helped negotiate a treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-creek">Lower Creek</a>. In 1734 he travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> with Oglethorpe and met King George II. He remained an ally of the colony until his death in 1739.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tomochichi.jpg" alt="Tomochichi" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Asarelah at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomochichi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
